1wlv|n|To weigh or lay out; to dispose of; to part with; as, to spend money for clothing. ; To bestow; to employ; -- often with on or upon. ; To consume; to waste; to squander; to exhaust; as, to spend an estate in gaming or other vices. ; To pass, as time; to suffer to pass away; as, to spend a day idly; to spend winter abroad. ; To exhaust of force or strength; to waste; to wear away; as, the violence of the waves was spent. ; To expend money or any other possession; to consume, use, waste, or part with, anything; as, he who gets easily spends freely. ; To waste or wear away; to be consumed; to lose force or strength; to vanish; as, energy spends in the using of it. ; To be diffused; to spread. ; To break ground; to continue working.	a:lzo,22,45;28uh,17,2;dow,4,2~lzo,22,45;dow,4,2;28uh,17,2	N:5cw,4,6;5bv,1,3~5cw,4,6;5bv,1,3
