1wv4|n|A long, slender, pointed rod, usually of iron, for holding meat while roasting. ; A small point of land running into the sea, or a long, narrow shoal extending from the shore into the sea; as, a spit of sand. ; The depth to which a spade goes in digging; a spade; a spadeful. ; To thrust a spit through; to fix upon a spit; hence, to thrust through or impale; as, to spit a loin of veal. ; To spade; to dig. ; To eject from the mouth; to throw out, as saliva or other matter, from the mouth. ; To eject; to throw out; to belch. ; The secretion formed by the glands of the mouth; spitle; saliva; sputum.	a:21e8,12,5~21e8,12,5	v:up1,10,3~up1,10,3	V:64w,114,3~64w,114,3
