1wyd|n|That which is taken from another by violence; especially, the plunder taken from an enemy; pillage; booty. ; Public offices and their emoluments regarded as the peculiar property of a successful party or faction, to be bestowed for its own advantage; -- commonly in the plural; as to the victor belong the spoils. ; That which is gained by strength or effort. ; The act or practice of plundering; robbery; aste. ; Corruption; cause of corruption. ; The slough, or cast skin, of a serpent or other animal.	N:163q,29,1~163q,29,1
